 "q-73377" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x+7}{(x+4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, what is the value of $A\\cdot B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+7 & =A(x+4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+7 & =A(-4+4)+B \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+7 & =A(0+4)+3 \\\\ 7 & =4A+3 \\\\ 4 & =4A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B=1\\cdot 3=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73377/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0d98b82-24d2-5b2c-b596-0300778bd187"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73377"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346806/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2cc0f2a4-2113-51e5-b911-2fc4173260db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346806/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "50b216c3-6c77-5f83-a661-2b960439eb1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346806/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2329c874-ee8f-5c9d-83d4-87658af4418f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346806/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-346806/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-346806/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346806/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5938315a-c866-573c-8a13